---
title: Art Blog
permalink: /art-blog/
accent: art
backLabel: Back to main site
description: Photography, pixel art and vector art by Zewei (Jason) Wu; landscapes, architecture and astrophotography.
tags: ["standalone"]
order: 2
---
{% extends "standalone.njk" %}
{% import "partials/figure.njk" as f %}
{% import "partials/icons.njk" as icons %}

{% block topnav %}
<nav class="topbar__nav" aria-label="Art sections">
  <a class="topbar__link" href="#welcome" data-section-link="welcome">Welcome</a>
  {%- for group in collections.artBySection %}
  <a class="topbar__link" href="#{{ group.slug }}" data-section-link="{{ group.slug }}">{{ group.section }}</a>
  {%- endfor %}
</nav>
{% endblock %}

{% block topend %}
<ul class="topbar__socials">
  <li><a href="https://www.instagram.com/jwu_arts/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Instagram — art">{{ icons.icon("palette", "Instagram (art)") }}</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.instagram.com/jasonwu_21/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" title="Instagram — photography">{{ icons.icon("camera", "Instagram (photography)") }}</a></li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}

{% block page %}
<div class="prose">

  <header class="page-head" id="welcome">
    <h1 class="page-head__title">Art</h1>
    <p class="page-head__intro">
      I am an enthusiast photographer who mostly enjoys landscape and travel photography.
      You can see different categories of my works listed here in reverse chronological order,
      including both photography and digital art pieces. Additionally, I post some of the pieces
      on my instagram (<a href="https://www.instagram.com/jwu_arts/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@jwu_arts</a>)
      account, so feel free to give it a follow if you are interested in seeing more or
      full-resolution versions of my works.
    </p>
  </header>

  {%- for group in collections.artBySection %}
  <section class="art-section">
    <h2 id="{{ group.slug }}">{{ group.section }}</h2>

    {%- if group.section == "Photography" %}
    <p>Landscapes and architecture photography let me explore how human history and nature intersect, framing stories through the textures of old cities and sweeping views of timeless scenes.</p>
    <p>I started out with a Nikon D750 DSLR camera, paired with a 50-year-old 50mm manual-focus lens gifted by a friend – a setup that lasted me for years. Throughout my photographic journey, I've also used other digital cameras from Canon, Sony, Fujifilm, and others – but Nikon's pairing remained my favorite for its versatility, vintage-feel, anc accurate color representation.</p>
    <p>Lately I've picked up film photography again after missing the dark room for ten years. Analog is such a physical medium that instantly allows me to recall the moment unlike anything in digital. Stay tuned for more experiments with film!</p>
    {%- elif group.section == "Digital Art" %}
    <p>Pixel art is easily my favorite style. I believe its minimalism is key for inspiring creativity and universality in the digital age. Similarly, vector art allows me to fuse my appreciation for technology into artistic expressions.</p>
    {%- endif %}

    {%- for bucket in group.years %}
    <h3 class="year-rule" id="{{ group.slug }}-{{ bucket.year }}">{{ bucket.year }}</h3>

    {%- for piece in bucket.items %}
    <article class="entry">
      {{ f.figure(piece.data.image, piece.data.alt or piece.data.title, piece.data.gear) }}
      <div class="entry__body">
        <h3 class="entry__title">{{ piece.data.title }}</h3>
        {%- if piece.data.category %}<p class="entry__meta">{{ piece.data.category }}</p>{% endif %}
        {{ piece.templateContent | safe }}
      </div>
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
    {%- endfor %}
  </section>
  {%- endfor %}

  {%- if not collections.artBySection.length %}
  <p class="empty-note">No art pieces yet. Add markdown files to <code>src/art-blog/pieces/</code>, or run <code>npm run new:art</code>.</p>
  {%- endif %}

</div>
{% endblock %}
